<title>MEXICO: ICA sees $150 mln from railroad concession.</title>
<headline>ICA sees $150 mln from railroad concession.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican builder Empresas ICA hopes to obtain $150 million in revenue over the coming four years from construction work on the Pacific-North railroad concession, a company source said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Our part of the payment (for the concession) is about $68 million, but we are most interested in the civil engineering side, for wich we expect revenues of some $150 million,&quot; an ICA director told Reuters, who asked not to be named.</p>
<p>The Mexican government granted the concession to run its Pacific-Northern railroad route on June 26 to ICA along with mining company Grupo Mexico and U.S. firm Union Pacific.</p>
<p>ICA has a 13-percent share in the consortium.</p>
<p>((--Daniel Perez, Monterrey bureau +528 345 7617))</p>
